## US-001 -- Role strings accept `--` (2026-11-26)

- `ParsedRole.extraArgs?:string[]` holds the tokens after `--`.
  `parseRoleString` turns on yargs `populate--` and reads
  `parsed['--']`; the field is set only when non-empty, so a role
  with no `--` (or a trailing bare `--`) deep-equals what it did
  before.
- `renderRoleString` appends ` -- <args>` when extraArgs is
  non-empty; `parseRoleString(renderRoleString(r))` round-trips.
- Assumption: the story says a stray positional before `--` throws
  the "Extra positional argument" error. In practice `.strict()`
  rejects it first with "Unknown argument: <tok>" (true before this
  change too, which is why the old test matches either). Behaviour
  is unchanged; the new test uses the same either-or regex.
- Gotcha: `mergeRoleWithCli` builds a fresh object and drops
  extraArgs. That is US-003's job (resolveRoles merge rules).
- Gotcha: tapzero's `t.throws` must be awaited in an async test, or
  a missing throw does not fail the test.
- docs/INDEX.md does not exist in this repo; the session prompt
  asked to study it. Nothing to read there.
- Verification: config tests 108/108, lint clean, build (tsc)
  clean. The full `npm test` went red on three runs, each time on
  a different set of timing-bound CLI subprocess tests in
  integration / review-integration (30s spawnCli timeouts, exit
  143; the 20s "round 2 reviewer started" wait). The machine's
  load average was 170-230 from other processes. The base commit
  passed those suites once at a lower load. The flakiest one
  (interrupted run resumes at the next round) passed 3/3 when run
  alone with this change. No test outside config.test.ts uses
  `--` in a role string, and a role string with no `--` parses to
  the same object as before. Treat these as load flakes. If the
  suite is red in a later session, check `uptime` first.
- Gotcha: `test` from test/shard.ts has no `.only`. To run one
  test, the copy must import `test` from
  '@substrate-system/tapzero' as well as switch it to `test.only`.

## US-002 -- The CLI accepts `--` (2026-11-26)

- The default command's builder sets
  `parserConfiguration({ 'populate--': true })`; the handler
  passes `readExtraArgs(argv['--'])` to `runExecute`, which hands
  it to `resolveRoles` as `CliOptions.extraArgs`. resolveRoles
  ignores it until US-003. Setting the config inside the builder
  is enough: argv['--'] is filled for the default command, and
  init/graph keep yargs' default `--` handling.
- New `readExtraArgs(dashDash:unknown):string[]` in src/config.ts
  is the one reader of a yargs `--` list, shared by
  `parseRoleString` and the CLI. yargs coerces numeric tokens
  after `--` to numbers even with populate-- on (`-- 7` gives
  `[7]`), so it maps each entry back to a string.
- Gotcha: yargs never ran `.strict()` or the positional checks on
  tokens after `--`, even before this change (they went to
  `argv._` and were dropped). So the CLI integration tests
  (`pi --dry-run -- --no-skills`, and `--` followed by unknown
  flags, stray positionals and `--timeout abc`) passed before the
  change too. The red step for this story was the unit test for
  `readExtraArgs`. The flags only become observable on the spawned
  argv (US-004) and in implementStr (US-003).
- Verification: config tests 111/111, the two new integration
  tests pass alone, lint clean, build (tsc) clean, full `npm test`
  green on the first run (load average ~110).

## US-003 -- resolveRoles merges extra args (2026-11-26)

- `resolveRoles` is the one place that decides extra args. With a
  CLI provider, implement.extraArgs is the CLI's list only. With
  none, it is the implement role string's list then the CLI's.
  review.extraArgs is always its own role string's list; CLI
  extras never reach it.
- `mergeRoleWithCli` now keeps the role's own extraArgs (it used
  to drop them) but never adds `cli.extraArgs`, since the review
  role goes through it too. CLI extras are appended in
  resolveRoles by the private `withExtraArgs`, which leaves
  extraArgs unset when the merged list is empty. Existing
  deepEqual tests on roles with no extras still pass unchanged.
- implementStr: with a CLI provider (or no config) it is
  `renderRoleString(implement)`, as before, now with the extras.
  With a config and no CLI extras it is still the config string
  verbatim, which already holds the role's own extras. With a
  config and CLI extras it is `renderRoleString` of the config
  role (not the CLI-filled merge) plus the merged extras.
  Assumption: re-rendering only the config role's own flags keeps
  the log line close to what the user wrote in .redeye.json.
- Gotcha: when running one integration test from a `test.only`
  copy, run node from the repo root (`node dist/test/x.test.js`),
  not from inside dist/test. Running from dist/test makes the
  timeout test fail for reasons that have nothing to do with the
  change, which looks like a regression.
- Verification: config tests 124/124 (9 new asserts red first),
  lint clean, build (tsc) clean. Full `npm test` at load average
  110-170: run 1 failed the 6s-timeout test in integration
  ("agent killed at the timeout keeps its committed and
  uncommitted work"), which passed 2/2 alone with this change.
  Run 2 passed that, but integration slice 9/20 crashed on the
  1s-timeout spawnAgent grandchild test (ENOENT on
  grandchild.pid, because the agent was killed before the
  grandchild wrote it). That slice passed 2/2 alone at load ~150.
  Neither test goes through resolveRoles. Every suite passed in
  at least one full run.

## US-004 -- spawnAgent forwards extra args (2026-11-26)

- `spawnAgent` takes an optional `extraArgs:string[]`. It is
  pushed onto argv after every flag redeye builds (provider args,
  --model, --max-turns, --thinking/--effort, codex's -c) and
  before pi's `@<prompt file>`, so the prompt stays last. Each
  entry is its own argv entry passed to `spawn` with no shell, so
  spaces and `$` reach the harness verbatim. Absent or empty
  extraArgs leaves the argv exactly as before for every provider.
  No caller passes it yet (US-005 to US-007).
- For hermes the extras land after `chat --query-file - --quiet`
  and --model, so only chat options work there (README note is
  US-008).
- New fake key `FAKE_PI_ARGV_LOG` in test/mock-agent-pi.js: it
  appends the fake pi's argv as one JSON array per run. Only
  test/orchestrator.test.ts sets it, and it is in that file's
  `FAKE_ENV_KEYS`.
- Tests (test/orchestrator.test.ts): a `spawnedArgv` helper
  spawns the fake once per call with model, maxTurns and effort
  set and returns each logged argv. Claude's argv with extras is
  the plain argv plus the extras; pi's is the plain argv minus
  the prompt file, plus the extras, then `@...`; empty extraArgs
  gives the plain argv. Pi argvs are compared up to the last
  entry, since the prompt file name is random per spawn.
- Verification: the three new tests went red (5 failed asserts)
  then green 8/8 alone; lint clean; build (tsc) clean. Full
  `npm test` at load average ~100-140: every suite passed except
  integration slice 9/20, which crashed on the same 1s-timeout
  grandchild.pid ENOENT flake US-003 recorded. That slice passed
  42/42 twice alone. That test never passes extraArgs.

