  both review-pass spawns pass their own role's list
  (`reviewer.extraArgs`, `fixer.extraArgs`). The roles are fields
  of `ReviewPassOpts`, so the options carry the extras.
- Assumption (the AC names one shared field on the options): the
  end-of-run reviewer is the adversarial review role when one is
  configured, possibly a different provider, so one shared list
  would hand implement's extras to the review harness, against
  US-007's intent. Per-role lists keep the two apart.
